  "title": "Sunday Tuoyo",
  "content": "Sunday Esijolomi Tuoyo (24 February 1935 – 17 December 2022) was a Nigerian Brigadier General who served as the Military Governor of Ondo State (July 1978 – October 1979) during the military regime of General Olusegun Obasanjo.\n\n\n== Education ==\nTuoyo attended Hussey College Warri.\n\n\n== Personal life ==\nTuoyo was of Itsekiri origin.\nHis son-in-law was Emmanuel Uduaghan, elected governor of Delta State in April 2007.\nHe died on 17 December 2022, at the age of 87.\n\n\n== References ==",
